Z||000024||artherd||12-15-2001||08:10 AM||||DKOV-  Some people just *don't* get it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>See the comments on 'yeah, but you only make power at 6200rpm' <P>When are they going to learn that (torque * RPM) / 5252 == horsepower!?<P>PS: Predator, trust me, get a TEC-II and just go drive the car.  They're what, $1700 or so on the street? It WILL solve all your engine management problems, and get the absolute most out of your engine!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000025||DKOV||12-15-2001||04:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88-DOHC:<BR><B> <BR>No a Supercharged 3.4 DOHC would be sex on wheels.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I thought I had read somewhere that swx on wheels, especially Fiero wheels, can kill you!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000026||DKOV||12-15-2001||04:02 PM||||By the way... "swx" is sex with a twist   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000027||lou_dias||12-15-2001||06:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR>See the comments on 'yeah, but you only make power at 6200rpm' <P>When are they going to learn that (torque * RPM) / 5252 == horsepower!?<BR>Ben<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know how it works but if you had a choice of making 220 hp @ 6200 rpm or 210 hp @ 5000 rpm with alot less headaches, what choice would you make?<P>the more you make at the top, the more you lose at the bottom...<BR>if you don't want a daily driver then build your 300hp DOHC...||||reg||1
Z||000028||artherd||12-15-2001||09:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou_dias:<BR><B> I know how it works but if you had a choice of making 220 hp @ 6200 rpm or 210 hp @ 5000 rpm with alot less headaches, what choice would you make?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Easy, give me the 6-grander!<P>But I like engines that make power, AND rev.<P>Shifting at 5grand bores me.  If I wanted 1,000lb-ft off the line, I'd get a dissel.<P>Then again, some people get a kick out of being able to light their tyres off idle at part-throttle, I'm just not one of them.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: Turbo kludgefest on a 3.4, or a STOCK TDC swap?  Neither one will swap in over the weekend, but we've got a fourm member here with each, and who's got the headaches?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000029||DKOV||12-15-2001||11:46 PM||||I'm not really sure what the issue here really is...  The difference of 10 HP over 1K revs?  That's like the difference between having your windows open or closed while driving.  Only the WINDOWS are more noticible.<P>My DOHC is totally a daily.  I have ZERO problems with it at idle, off the line, to and from the store, at the track or on the freeway...  What exactly is it that you think goes wrong with this motor at high HP?<P>The thing runs GREAT at all RPMs and still winds to the moon.  I don't think I get the argument here...<P>Given the same exact Fiero, putting the 3.4 DOHC makes more sense simply because of the HEAT involved.  The difference in HP is not significant and by your statement, the power comes on later in the revs (which I don't agree with) which is the SAME as a Turbo.<P>This motor has SO MUCH torque, I can spin the tires into 3rd gear if I wanted to and I have once or twice, but spinning tires doesn't get you to 60 any faster.<P>You see, I own a Lotus Esprit Turbo too.  That car is Hella Fast (0 - 60 in 4.4 and to 100 in 9.8) so I am VERY familiar what a Turbo feels like, but I am also familiar with the headaches and maintenance that coms along with them.<P>Given the option, if my Lotus was normally aspirated and made the same HP, I'd take that over the Turbo in a heartbeat.  Lotus does not, however, make that kind of HP without one so...<P>Having the 3.4 DOHC has really been enlightening.  Normally Aspirated HP comes on sooner and can be easier to maintain.  The "turbo lag" normally associated with Turbo Charged cars is gone and I still get the big HP coming around 3K and up which is the very SAME curve as my Lotus.<P>Don't get me wrong, I LOOOOVE my Lotus!  One of the most exciting cars I own.  Nothing in existance can out handle that thing.  But I do like my Fiero too.<P>I suppose that a guy could put a Turbo on a 2.8 or a Pushrod by why sacrifice the HP and performance?  I WANT that kind of power.  I don't want to cut myself short some 30+ ponies just because I want to say the word "turbo" when talking about my car...<P>I take that back, I like using "turbo" in sentences like...  "Just smoked a Turbo..."  or  "flamed a Turbo..." or "what's that car dropping behind me in traffic?  Oh, it's a Turbo..."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Seriously, to each his own.  For me, if the best of both words can be had, it's a well tuned 3.4 DOHC.  Plain.  Simple.<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000030||lou_dias||12-16-2001||11:25 AM||||Well, I think we've all gone a little off topic maybe then...<P>I though we were discussing the +'s and -'s of going with a pushrod 3.4 turbo to 300hp or building a 3.4 dohc NA to 300hp<P>somehow it turned into comparing to the engines in stock form but if you re-read my posts, they might make more sense now...||||reg||1
Z||000031||DKOV||12-16-2001||01:39 PM||||I would think, then, a pushrod 3.4 w ould definately losse the low end if pushed to 300 HP...  It has a much larger gap to cover than a 3.4 DOHC.  80 HP is not hard to come by.<P>A 2.8 on the other hand, would absolutely HAVE to have a Turbo to compete.<P>Of course, my 2.2 is there with the assistance of a Turbo so I guess if a guy could manage the proper launch...<P>Just as a note, there ARE some applications for the 3.4 DOHC with a Turbo.  I've seen them myself and even took some snapsots.  I think the motor I was looking as was only running around 6 - 9 lbs of boost but pushing out close to 400 HP.  Pretty amazing, I'd say.<P>Eventually, they bumped the boost to 11 lbs to get some more ponies and blew the thing.  Bummer.<P>I'd say that is the drawback to this whole deal.  The 3.4 DOHC can take a Turbo but as with everything... IN MODERATION  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -<P>||||reg||1
